# Docker build context exclusions (root). Started in TEACH-28 for agent-skill directories;
# TEACH-24 (Railway Dockerfile for api/worker/migrate) extends it.
#
# The Dockerfile's `pruner` stage copies the whole context and runs `turbo prune`, so this file
# decides what is uploaded, not what ships. MUST stay in the context: root package.json, bun.lock,
# bunfig.toml, turbo.json, every workspace package.json / tsconfig*.json, all src/, and
# packages/db/drizzle/** (migration SQL + meta journal), infra/docker/entrypoint.sh.
#
# Agent skills and agent guides (ADR 0017): never needed in an image.
**/.agents
**/.claude
**/.opencode
**/skills-lock.json
**/AGENTS.md

# Dependencies, VCS, secrets, build outputs, caches, local data.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.gitignore
.env*
**/.env*
dist
**/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo
coverage
**/coverage
.data
.railway

# Not part of the api/worker image: the SPA, the design system, docs, CI, tests, tooling.
# (packages/storage IS part of it: @tj/api's GET /files/:key proxy bundles the StorageAdapter.)
# turbo prune must still see every workspace's manifest to resolve the graph + lockfile, so the
# package.json of each excluded workspace is re-included (their sources are not).
apps/web/**
!apps/web/package.json
packages/ui/**
!packages/ui/package.json
packages/api-client/**
!packages/api-client/package.json
docs
.github
infra/postgres
infra/railway
infra/README.md
**/*.test.ts
**/*.md
**/test
**/tests
**/e2e
**/playwright*
scripts
lefthook.yml
commitlint.config.ts
biome.json
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
